# A contributor's global ignore file can carry patterns that happen to match a
# directory this repository owns, silently excluding source. Re-including every
# tree makes the repository's own layout authoritative regardless of what a
# personal ignore file says. Kept in step with the tree by the source-tracked
# gate, which derives its list from the directories that exist.

!agents/**
!applications/**
!boot/**
!brand/**
!communications/**
!compat/**
!core/**
!design/**
!emulator/**
!examples/**
!graphics/**
!hardware/**
!infrastructure/**
!input/**
!ipc/**
!kernel/**
!media/**
!networking/**
!packaging/**
!runtimes/**
!sdk/**
!security/**
!services/**
!session/**
!shell/**
!simulator/**
!storage/**
!store/**
!test-vectors/**
!tests/**
!tools/**

# Documentation, except the specification, which is local-only for now.
!docs/**
/docs/PLATFORM_SPEC.md

# External design reference — never commit
*Tour.html

# Local-only engineering instruction — reference, never commit
/docs/APPLICATION_LAYER.md
/docs/Agent-integration.md
/docs/No-Gated-On-You.md

# Rendered frames written to the repo root by the render steps are build output
/home.png
/frame.png
/icons.png
/screen.png

# Live session frames written by `zig build run`
/session_*.png
/shell.png
/motion_*.png

# rendered artifacts — build outputs, never source
out.png
tour.png
*.render.png
avOS
avOSTour.html
# Developer-local config (design reference path, etc.) — never commit
.local/

# Vendored engine cache: rebuilt from engines.lock.json by `zig build vendor-engines`.
.engines/

# Downloaded engine archives: the fetch cache `vendor-engines` re-verifies against the pin.
.engine-archives/

# Icon PNG artifacts — regenerated by tools/icon-build, never hand-committed
/design/icons/generated/
